silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_01_probe_catus_collision_concrete_anchor_1#catusbareepithet silm:hasLongDescription "The CatusBareEpithet is The bare species epithet \"catus\" as a prose string; not a typed node in O_01; no representable functor; forbidden from carrying an identification arrow to Mittens. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'catus', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
